  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shaikh Tousib Bilal vs The State Of Maharashtra And Another on 26 August, 2024 2024:Bhc-Aug:19287 1 46-ABA-1272-24.odt In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad Anticipatory Bail Application No. 1272 Of 2024 Shaikh Tousib Bilal Versus The State Of Maharashtra And Another ... Advocate for Applicant : Mr. Sartaj Khan H. Pathan App for Respondents : Ms. P. V. Diggikar ... Coram : S. G. Mehare, J. Date : 26-08-2024 Per Court :- 1.",
    "facts": "2. The applicant seeks pre-arrest bail in Crime No.I-177 of 2024 registered with Begumpura Police Station, Aurangabad, for the offences punishable under Sections 328, 272, 273, 188 of the Indian Penal Code and Sections 26(1), 26(2)(iv), 30(2)(a), 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. The police found scented Gutka in the vehicle. It was prohibited to transport and sell in the State of Maharashtra. The co-accused gave the information to the police that the so-called seized scented gutka was purchased from the applicant. However, he did not inform the police about the details of the godown, etc. of the applicant. The police visited the address given by the co-accused, Shaikh Tousib Bilal vs The State Of Maharashtra And Another on 26 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/122522166/ 1 but the applicant was not there. The police have a suspicion 2 46-ABA-1272-24.odt against the applicant on the basis of the statement by co-accused. Except this, there is no direct evidence against the applicant. The issue of application of Section 328 of the Indian Penal Code in many cases, whether it would attract in the cases of selling and transporting the scented gutka, is seized with the Hon'ble Supreme Court.",
    "arguments": "",
